  "body": "This might be more nitpicking that anything else but, I do wonder whether one wants to \"normalize\" the writing of HTML this way?\r\n\r\nI know that it is completely valid to not close these list elements but, I do feel it would be better if the examples in the docs follow general best practice.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/5712d1313842e8c085f2a942dbf5060e24ff0ee1/#the-ol-element\r\n\r\n> &lt;p&gt;I have lived in the following countries \\(given in the order of when\r\n> I first lived there\\):​&lt;/p&gt;\r\n> &lt;ol&gt;\r\n>  &lt;li&gt;Switzerland\r\n>  &lt;li&gt;United Kingdom\r\n>  &lt;li&gt;United States\r\n>  &lt;li&gt;Norway\r\n> &lt;/ol&gt;",
